# Copy to .env and fill in. Only .env.example is committed; .env is ignored.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed variables reach the app, and the Expo CLI INLINES them into the bundle
# at build time -- they are readable in plain text in any shipped build, so nothing secret belongs
# here. There is only one value, and it is public by nature: the address the app calls.
#
# Google and Facebook sign-in need no configuration in the app. Both are browser flows the API owns
# end to end, so their client ids and secrets live in the API's configuration (Google:ClientId /
# Google:ClientSecret, Facebook:AppId / Facebook:AppSecret, set via dotnet user-secrets).
#
# Values are read at bundle time, so reload the app after changing them. For a machine-specific
# override use .env.local, which takes precedence and is ignored too.

# Where hovante.api lives, including the /api/v1 prefix. On a device or in Expo Go, localhost is
# the PHONE, not your computer -- use your machine's LAN IP (http://10.0.0.8:5179/api/v1) or an
# https tunnel to test on hardware. Defaults to http://localhost:5179/api/v1 when unset.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
